{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"As of **6 November 2026**:\n\n- **Mixed umbrella:** Apply the “UCITS ETF” identifier to the relevant ETF sub-fund(s), not indiscriminately to the umbrella or its non-ETF sibling sub-funds.\n- **Sub-fund with ETF and unlisted classes:** Ireland permits the identifier at the **listed ETF share-class level**, without requiring it in the common sub-fund name or the names of unlisted classes. Relevant documentation and marketing should clearly distinguish those classes.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Classification and naming differ. Under ESMA’s definition, a sub-fund with at least one qualifying ETF class is a UCITS ETF for regulatory purposes. That does **not** make its unlisted classes exchange-traded, or turn other sub-funds in the umbrella into ETFs."}}
